{
  "spec": "LXMF-rust/DISPLAY_NAMES.md sections 2.1 and 10: the Retichat field 0xD1 and the group transition",
  "notes": [
    "All *_hex values are raw msgpack bytes as lowercase hex. The same file is run by LXMF-rust (tests/retichat_field_vectors.rs), Retichat-ios, Retichat-android and Retichat-js.",
    "keys: the Retichat field's keys. key is the integer key inside the 0xD1 map; name is the JSON name used in decode[].group; type is name | str | bool; legacy_field is the old top-level field number (decimal: 160 = 0xA0 ... 168 = 0xA8), null for key 0.",
    "decode: state / display_name decode the name (key 0 of the 0xD1 map) exactly as display_name_vectors.json decode_field: state is absent | clear | name, display_name is set only for state name. A 0xD1 that is not a map is ignored whole.",
    "decode: group has all nine group entries, always present; each is a JSON string (str entries), true/false (group_relay_done) or null when absent.",
    "Reader rule (section 10): each group entry comes from the 0xD1 map when the map holds that key with the entry's type; otherwise from its old top-level field when that holds the entry's type; otherwise null. An empty str or false in the map is a value and wins.",
    "Types are strict: a str entry is a msgpack str (bin is not a str), group_relay_done is a msgpack bool. Nil or any other type counts as not there.",
    "Keys (top-level field numbers and keys inside the map) are integers of any msgpack width (positive fixint, uint8/16/32/64, int8/16/32/64 holding a non-negative value). String keys and negative keys never match. Unknown keys are ignored.",
    "No vector holds a duplicate key or a str with invalid UTF-8 in a group entry: readers need not agree on those.",
    "encode: the two send forms, starting from the fields map start_hex and setting entries in list order (key is the Retichat key, value a JSON string or bool). legacy_hex is the old form (top-level 0xA0-0xA8, appended in set order, a repeated key replaced in place); retichat_hex the new form (entries in the 0xD1 map, ascending key order, 0xD1 appended when absent). Writers emit the shortest msgpack forms. GROUP_ENTRIES_IN_RETICHAT_FIELD (Swift: groupEntriesInRetichatField) selects the form; it is false until the switch around 2026-10-26."
  ],
